            "passageText": "Agricultural crop rotation maintains soil fertility and controls pest populations naturally. By alternating crop species in a field across seasons, farmers disrupt insect life cycles and prevent nutrient exhaustion. For instance, planting nitrogen-fixing legumes replenishes soil nitrogen levels depleted by heavy grain crops like corn and wheat.",
