            "passageText": "Ice core samples extracted from polar ice sheets provide paleoclimatologists with ancient atmospheric gas samples preserved over hundreds of thousands of years. As annual snow compresses into dense ice, atmospheric gas bubbles become trapped. Analyzing oxygen and hydrogen isotope ratios reveals past polar temperatures, while measuring greenhouse gas levels in trapped bubbles indicates historical carbon dioxide concentrations.",
