            "passageText": "Behavioral economists have shown that human decision-making frequently diverges from rational economic models. Cognitive heuristics, such as loss aversion and anchoring, influence financial choices. Loss aversion describes the psychological phenomenon where individuals feel the emotional pain of a financial loss twice as intensely as the pleasure of an equivalent gain.",
